- Use a combination of metrics that cover different aspects of productivity.
- Ensure that the metrics are measurable, achievable, relevant, and time-bound (SMART).
- Regularly review and adjust the metrics based on feedback and performance data to avoid bias and keep the assessment relevant and effective.
- Consider using third-party assessment tools or consultants to bring in external objectivity and expertise in evaluating productivity metrics.

